message: "If you use this project or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "AUGUR: The Effective Epistemic Date of Time-Locked Language Models"
authors:
  - family-names: "Syed"
    given-names: "Zaid Ali"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4313-1510"
version: 1.0.4
date-released: 2026-10-21
url: "https://github.com/zaidwhy/augur"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zaidwhy/augur"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22309658"
abstract: >
  Time-locked language models do not stand at their knowledge cutoff.
  This project measures where they actually speak from, and whether
  they can be moved - including the finding that a model trained on
  nothing published after 1938 self-reports the year as 1899 (1900 on
  a re-run). Version 1.0.4 withdraws the elicitation-framing finding
  of earlier versions and adds the re-run transcripts.
